From: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: add a mem_profile module parameter

ath12k picks the firmware memory profile from the RAM Linux sees: the
smaller 512 MiB profile below 512 MiB, the default otherwise. A board whose
firmware cannot run the default budget with the memory it was given has no
way to ask for the smaller one without capping Linux's RAM.

Add mem_profile=auto|low: auto keeps the existing choice, low selects the
512 MiB profile (fewer VAPs and clients per radio) whatever the RAM size.

Signed-off-by: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -34,6 +34,10 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(ftm_mode, "Boots up in factory test mode");
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(ath12k_ftm_mode);
 
+static char *ath12k_mem_profile = "auto";
+module_param_named(mem_profile, ath12k_mem_profile, charp, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(mem_profile, "Firmware memory profile: auto (by RAM size) or low (512 MiB)");
+
 /* protected with ath12k_hw_group_mutex */
 static struct list_head ath12k_hw_group_list = LIST_HEAD_INIT(ath12k_hw_group_list);
 
@@ -1806,6 +1810,12 @@
 	unsigned long total_ram;
 	struct sysinfo si;
 
+	/* A board whose firmware cannot run the default budget with the
+	 * memory it was given can ask for the smaller profile explicitly.
+	 */
+	if (ath12k_mem_profile && !strcmp(ath12k_mem_profile, "low"))
+		return ATH12K_QMI_MEMORY_MODE_LOW_512_M;
+
 	si_meminfo(&si);
 	total_ram = si.totalram * si.mem_unit;
 
